{"id":"htan-the-cellular-geography-of-therapeutic-resistance-in-cancer","title":"The Cellular Geography of Therapeutic Resistance in Cancer","short_title":"HTA5","aliases":["HTA5"],"summary":"Of the fourteen HTAN atlases, this is the one whose stated purpose is resistance: mapping where in a tumor resistant cells survive treatment. It carries 20,350 files across multiplexed tissue imaging, single-cell RNA sequencing and bulk DNA, and it is the only atlas in the network carrying the extended clinical data tier alongside therapy, follow-up, exposure, family history and molecular test components.\nIt is also the clearest case in this corpus of a resource that is well built and apparently unused. HTAN maintains its own publication manifest, and this atlas has no entry in it - unlike most atlases, which record three to five publications. The combination of a resistance-focused design, unusually complete clinical annotation and no recorded downstream use makes it the strongest reuse opportunity we identified.","one_liner":"An HTAN atlas built explicitly around therapeutic resistance, with multiplexed imaging, single-cell RNA sequencing and the richest clinical annotation of any atlas here - and no publications recorded in the network's own manifest.","identifiers":[{"scheme":"accession_other","value":"HTA5","url":"https://humantumoratlas.org/explore?selectedFilters=%5B%7B%22value%22%3A%22HTA5%22%7D%5D","is_primary":true,"evidence":[{"method":"api","source_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncihtan/htan-portal/master/data/syn_metadata.json","source_label":"HTAN portal metadata (ncihtan/htan-portal)","retrieved_at":"2026-09-18T02:46:11.906526Z","snippet":null,"locator":"atlas HTA5","confidence":"high","reviewer":null,"reviewed_at":null,"note":null}]},{"scheme":"synapse_id","value":"syn39259236","url":"https://www.synapse.org/#!Synapse:syn39259236","is_primary":false,"evidence":[{"method":"api","source_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ncihtan/htan-portal/master/d